From: A50 port development
Subject: [PATCH] mirserver: retain physical-pixel DPR with UBports Mir1

UBports Mir1 ebc14fb still applies its 0007 patch which removes scale
division from DisplayConfigurationOutput::extents(). QtMir fbc50e5 exposes
screen.scale as native DPR while retaining those physical extents. That
scales the scene past the framebuffer and clips the shell. Retain the
previous DPR for this Mir1-only build. Do not change GRID_UNIT_PX, Mir's
advertised application scale, or the wizard's QML geometry.

QtMir main 38268ef explicitly rejects WITH_MIR2 builds. Remove this
compatibility patch once the Mir1/QtMir scaling transition is coordinated.

--- a/src/platforms/mirserver/platformscreen.cpp
+++ b/src/platforms/mirserver/platformscreen.cpp
@@ -339 +339,2 @@
-    m_devicePixelRatio = screen.scale; // FIXME: I need to announce this changing, probably by delete/recreate Screen
+    // UBports Mir1 returns physical extents, so native DPR must remain 1.
+    m_devicePixelRatio = 1.0;
